  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RDDP Rwanda Dairy Development Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Developing financial products is an assignment that requires a number of steps. To create an impact and allow for testing, ICCO-CORDAID advises to start with 14 SACCOS in the selected districts and 1 Microfinance Institution as a pilot. Thereafter but before the end of 2022, we should scale-up to the other SACCOs.  

The SACCOs differ in operations and functioning in terms of governance, liquidity and understanding of credit risk.  The automation of SACCOs is still at a low level. To develop a product that is adapted to these conditions and have staff that understands this product, we organise different trainings. Also, the Umurenge SACCOs will be amalgamated at district level in 2022 and 23. We expect that this restructuring will ease some of the work if we plan to start with the restructured ones.  

MFIs have better capacituy. The market assessment process will focus on the selected districts but the rest of the steps are done at the head office (Kigali) Once the MFI approves the new loan product, it will be used within all its branches so reaching clients in different districts.</narrative>
  </description>
